    "body": "Just noticed that even with my \"workaround\" of converting `PROMPT_COMMAND` to an array, `cmd_duration` breaks after running 2 commands. Updated title and GP.\n\n**edit:** actually there's nothing significant about \"2 commands\". It seems that when spawning a new shell (with the workaround above) iTerm's shell integration actually just doesn't get activated until the `min_time` has elapsed. After that, Starship's modules stop working.\n\r\n### Newly spawned shell\r\n```\r\n~ $ sleep 4\r\ntook 4s  ~ $ sleep 4\r\ntook 5s  ~ $ sleep 4\r\n~ $ sleep 4\r\n~ $ \r\n```\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
